1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,240
The Electric Train

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:19,640
And suddenly, the Earth is attacked by an alien spaceship.

3
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,820
If help arrives here on time, we'll be saved.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,840
Move faster, faster! Come on, get off the train! Move it, move it!

5
00:00:35,799 --> 00:00:38,439
Tom Thomas! We came here to play!

6
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:42,320
Ah, finally you're here! I need some aliens for this game.

7
00:00:42,679 --> 00:00:44,960
What kind of aliens are you talking about?

8
00:00:45,159 --> 00:00:48,000
Just plain old aliens. You know the ones.

9
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:51,000
They come to destroy the Earth and just about everything!

10
00:00:51,679 --> 00:00:53,879
We don't want to destroy anything at all!

11
00:00:54,039 --> 00:00:57,159
Why can't we be the train engineers?

12
00:00:57,159 --> 00:00:57,719
Huh?

13
00:00:58,119 --> 00:00:59,279
Train engineers?

14
00:00:59,959 --> 00:01:02,919
You don't know anything about driving a train.

15
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,039
Oh, we know plenty about trains!

16
00:01:08,039 --> 00:01:10,280
Humans invented the railroad long ago,

17
00:01:10,359 --> 00:01:13,079
but back then the rails were made out of wood.

18
00:01:13,679 --> 00:01:18,400
People didn't start making metal rails until the end of the 18th century.

19
00:01:18,719 --> 00:01:22,120
But the first railroad cars had no engines to give them their power,

20
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:25,319
instead they used horses to pull them along.

21
00:01:25,319 --> 00:01:28,959
Later, horses were replaced by the steam engine.

22
00:01:28,959 --> 00:01:33,439
Wood and coal would burn in their furnaces to boil the water in the boilers,

23
00:01:33,439 --> 00:01:35,839
making the steam that turned their wheels.

24
00:01:35,839 --> 00:01:38,759
And the Fixies were there to help those trains go,

25
00:01:39,039 --> 00:01:42,679
making sure all of the parts could work together smoothly.

26
00:01:44,399 --> 00:01:46,639
But now steam engines have long gone away.

27
00:01:46,639 --> 00:01:49,879
The railroad uses electricity now for its power.

28
00:01:49,879 --> 00:01:55,119
These electric trains race along the railway at almost the speed of an airplane.

29
00:01:55,319 --> 00:02:01,359
So you might know trains, but you'll still be the aliens.

30
00:02:01,659 --> 00:02:03,099
This railroad is mine.

31
00:02:03,399 --> 00:02:05,419
So you're going to play the way I want.

32
00:02:05,659 --> 00:02:08,400
The train is unloaded and leaving the station.

33
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:14,539
You can play choo-choo by yourself.

34
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:15,419
And I will.

35
00:02:17,719 --> 00:02:20,560
Pew, pew, pew, pew, pew, pew.

36
00:02:23,379 --> 00:02:23,859
Hmm.

37
00:02:25,319 --> 00:02:27,319
Hey, why did you stop?

38
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:36,319
This doesn't help either. It's not going at all.

39
00:02:37,319 --> 00:02:38,319
Simka!

40
00:02:40,319 --> 00:02:41,319
Nolik!

41
00:02:41,319 --> 00:02:44,319
Where are you? Did I hurt your feelings or something?

42
00:02:46,319 --> 00:02:48,319
Mom, is dad gonna be home soon?

43
00:02:48,319 --> 00:02:50,319
No, is something the matter?

44
00:02:50,319 --> 00:02:52,319
We've been attacked by evil aliens.

45
00:02:52,319 --> 00:02:54,319
The train has to be fixed right away

46
00:02:54,319 --> 00:02:56,120
Or we'll never escape them.

47
00:02:56,639 --> 00:02:59,199
Uh, mm-hmm? You want some tea?

48
00:03:00,319 --> 00:03:03,799
Ah, I've got to think of something.

49
00:03:05,199 --> 00:03:08,039
Simka, Nolik, I know you're in there.

50
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:11,180
Please forgive me if I hurt your feelings.

51
00:03:12,079 --> 00:03:13,379
I'm really sorry.

52
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:17,620
There's nobody but you that can save the world from the evil aliens.

53
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:22,139
All right, it talked us back into it.

54
00:03:22,139 --> 00:03:24,739
Well, let's go and check the rails.

55
00:03:24,739 --> 00:03:26,419
Nolik, follow me!

56
00:03:29,779 --> 00:03:31,059
I'm faster!

57
00:03:32,339 --> 00:03:33,019
Wow!

58
00:03:33,019 --> 00:03:35,019
Well, so much for being faster!

59
00:03:35,219 --> 00:03:37,019
But it looks like I found the brake!

60
00:03:37,539 --> 00:03:40,259
Tom Thomas, the rails are broken!

61
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,939
I know, and so?

62
00:03:42,939 --> 00:03:45,939
You know, but that's why your train is not running.

63
00:03:45,939 --> 00:03:52,659
Just like a real train, model trains run on electricity.

64
00:03:52,939 --> 00:03:56,819
But there aren't any batteries inside the locomotive to pull the other cars.

65
00:03:56,979 --> 00:04:00,060
The engine gets its electricity from the rails.

66
00:04:00,259 --> 00:04:02,780
Each piece of the rail has a wire in it.

67
00:04:02,979 --> 00:04:04,620
If the rails come apart,

68
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:08,579
the electricity can't flow through the track and get to the train.

69
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:12,979
And without electricity, the train's engine just stops going.

70
00:04:13,819 --> 00:04:16,860
So reconnect the rails and your train will run again!

71
00:04:21,019 --> 00:04:23,539
Uh-huh. Put them together.

72
00:04:24,539 --> 00:04:25,420
Yes!

73
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,420
Hurrah! The train is running!

74
00:04:30,019 --> 00:04:31,060
Way to go!

75
00:04:31,139 --> 00:04:32,539
So will you play with me now?

76
00:04:32,699 --> 00:04:34,620
And which way are we playing this time?

77
00:04:34,779 --> 00:04:36,259
Whatever you want, I'm with you!

78
00:04:37,699 --> 00:04:41,379
The train rushes down the track with Nolik as its engineer,

79
00:04:41,379 --> 00:04:44,779
when suddenly from out of the sky comes an alien spaceship!

80
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:54,060
Greetings to you, O people of planet Earth!

81
00:04:54,379 --> 00:04:58,060
I come from far away, from another galaxy!

82
00:04:58,659 --> 00:05:00,860
Have you come to destroy everything?

83
00:05:01,219 --> 00:05:05,019
No! I've come to fix it all!

